From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Richard Swanson <rswanson05@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 07:15:27 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] feat: let machine enable and disable take a label

enable and disable only accepted a profile ID, while status and
reconnect also accept the machine's label. find_machine now finds a
machine by ID or label without checking whether it is enabled, and
resolve_machine adds that check on top, so enable can find a disabled
machine by its label.

diff --git a/src/cli/machine.rs b/src/cli/machine.rs
index 2459805a..30610747 100644
--- a/src/cli/machine.rs
+++ b/src/cli/machine.rs
@@ -14,8 +14,8 @@ const HELP: &str = "Usage:
   herdr machine add <ssh-target> [--label <label>] [--remote-session <name>]
   herdr machine rename <profile-id> --label <label>
   herdr machine remove <profile-id>
-  herdr machine enable <profile-id>
-  herdr machine disable <profile-id>
+  herdr machine enable <label-or-id>
+  herdr machine disable <label-or-id>
 
 Add prepares the remote Herdr installation and starts its server before saving.
 Missing or incompatible installations require approval in an interactive terminal.
@@ -536,11 +536,18 @@ fn remove(args: &[String]) -> std::io::Result<i32> {
 
